<title>SWITZERLAND: WTO sets panel in Canada-EU beef hormone dispute.</title>
<headline>WTO sets panel in Canada-EU beef hormone dispute.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Trade Organisation on Wednesday agreed to set up a panel to examine a Canadian complaint that a European Union ban on the import of hormone- treated beef violates free trade rules.</p>
<p>The panel will be the second on the issue. In May, the WTO's Dispute Settlement Body (DSB), on which all members of the organisation can sit, agreed to a similar United States request.</p>
<p>Canadian sources told reporters that the two panels would have to run separately because hearings in the U.S. case had already begun.</p>
<p>Other countries who have reserved their rights to be associated with the U.S. complaint are Australia, New Zealand and Norway.</p>
</text>
